wrong[False False True]: Spaces, commas and the colon are skipped, and capitals are lowered: amanaplanacanalpanama reads the same both ways.
hint: Only letters are compared, in lower case.
hint: Write each phrase as its letters only.
right: `True False True`: amanaplanacanalpanama is a palindrome, raceacar isn't, and a string with no letters has nothing that can fail.
wrong: Strip each phrase to its letters, in lower case: amanaplanacanalpanama (a palindrome), raceacar (not one, since its reverse is racaecar), and nothing at all for "!!", which counts as True.

