hint: What does `[::-1]` create?
right: At most n // 2 comparisons, an early exit on the first mismatch, and no extra copy: O(n) time, O(1) space.
wrong: The check pairs the characters from the outside in, so it needs at most n // 2 comparisons, stops at the first mismatch, and copies nothing. Sorting isn't needed, and even lengths work too.

